---
/* CATEGORY — 16 Oct rework, client note: load and inspect
   vision-naire.com/pages/n-10, take its style for this page. Inspected
   live: a 2-column editorial grid on a dark ground, large lifestyle-scale
   images, caption reduced to name + price only (no size chips visible in
   the grid itself -- those live on the product page, which is the one
   place they're actually needed). Translated into this project's own
   system rather than copied: dark ground is already one of this system's
   three sanctioned grounds (DESIGN.md), not a new addition; type stays
   Archivo + Martian Mono, no new typeface borrowed from the reference.
   One representative example (Outerwear, placeholder data). No footer
   (client note, 16 Oct).

   17 Oct, client note: "that page is out of place and poor .. its also
   meant to have a hero like i reference with vision-naire.. i specified
   the page because of its hero and arrangements". Re-inspected n-10 --
   the part missed the first pass: above its product grid sits a hero
   that is PURE TYPE, not a photo -- the category name set at ~384px,
   pinned top-left right under the nav, with a one-line byline pinned near
   the bottom of the same tall block and a large empty gap between them.
   That's DESIGN.md's own "type as object" doctrine (Section 1/6: "one
   monumental type object anchors a screen") -- already this project's
   rule, just not yet applied here.

   17 Oct, second client note, same day: "remove '4 pieces .. updated
   weekly' .. the hero is a two column, word and image" -- the pure-type
   version above is overridden by this more specific instruction. The
   byline/meta line is gone; the word now shares the hero with an actual
   image column instead of standing alone against empty space. Still
   --t-display (this system's biggest token, not the reference's literal
   384px) -- the brief is "word and image", not "copy n-10 exactly". */
import Layout from '../../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Nav from '../../components/Nav.astro';
import DropsNotify from '../../components/DropsNotify.astro';

/* 17 Oct, client note: "make everything in naira.. lowest amount being
   13,000 Naira" -- same per-product price as shop.astro/all.astro. */
const products = [
  { name: 'Bushel Overshirt', price: '₦111,500' },
  { name: 'Ply Hoodie',       price: '₦87,500' },
  { name: 'Cue Cardigan',     price: '₦82,000' },
  { name: 'Panel Jacket',     price: '₦153,500' },
];
---
<Layout
  title="Outerwear | The Glow Tribe Shop"
  description="Outerwear — pieces made by the tribe, sold by the tribe."
  pageStylesHref="/styles/shop.css"
  bodyClass="shop"
>
  <Nav current="shop" ctaMuted />

  <main class="shop-dark shop-sub__top">
    <div class="shop-container" data-fade>
      <header class="shop-category-hero">
        <p class="shop-breadcrumb"><a href="/shop">Shop</a> / <a href="/shop/collections">Collections</a> / Outerwear</p>
        <div class="shop-category-hero__grid">
          <h1 class="shop-category-hero__name">Outerwear</h1>
          <div class="shop-category-hero__image"><span>Outerwear 4:5</span></div>
        </div>
      </header>
      <div class="shop-editorial-grid">
        {products.map(p => (
          <a class="shop-editorial-item" href="/shop/product">
            <div class="shop-editorial-item__slot"><span>Product 4:5</span></div>
            <div class="shop-editorial-item__cap">
              <span class="shop-editorial-item__name">{p.name}</span>
              <span class="shop-editorial-item__price">{p.price}</span>
            </div>
          </a>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <DropsNotify />
</Layout>
